  "finding": "Partial annotation. Only ds1 (555 of 5273 train images, 10.5%) labels rider and bike; ds2 (1070) never labels rider/bike and ds3 (3648) never labels rider, bike or number-plate. ds2/ds3 images visibly contain riders and motorcycles, so training treats them as background, which suppresses rider/bike recall. Test rider/bike recall is effectively measured only on ds1, and correct rider/bike predictions on ds2/ds3 test images count as false positives, so whole-split rider/bike precision is understated.",
